{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"depth of a module depth of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md","fileName":"Depth of a Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Depth of a Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Homological Algebra and Derived Functors]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Homological Algebra and Derived Functors","Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"depth of a module depth of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md","fileName":"Depth of a Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Depth of a Module","heading":"Depth of a Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The depth of a module M with respect to an ideal I is the maximum length of an M-regular sequence contained in I. Over a Noetherian local ring, depth usually refers to the maximal ideal.\n\nThe source also characterizes depth as the smallest degree in which Ext_R(R/I,M) is nonzero. Depth cannot exceed dimension and is linked to finite projective dimension by the [[Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Homological Algebra and Derived Functors","Auslander-Buchsbaum Formula","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"depth of a module depth of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Depth of a Module.md